        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-2992",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "3.10 — Components · Build Orchestrator",
          "documentation": "Inside build.mjs. One command per video, and the only place stages are run by code rather than by hand. Everything it decides — trims included — is measured, so a video can be rebuilt from the repo.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2993",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2992"
              },
              "name": "Manifest reader",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: videos/*.json\n\nThe parts in recording order, the env every stage gets, the crossfade and the silence to keep either side of a join. The only, no-record, join-only and no-gate flags pick what runs."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2994",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2992"
              },
              "name": "Part folders",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: paths.mjs · DEMO_OUT\n\nEach part builds in out/{video}/{part}/, so no take overwrites another's fixed-name stage files. The TTS clip cache stays shared."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2995",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2992"
              },
              "name": "Part runner",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: child processes\n\ndriver, assemble, project, compose, narrate, tighten and cards, in order, each with the part's folder and the manifest env. Prints the part's before-the-take note first."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2996",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2992"
              },
              "name": "Part gate",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: qa.mjs\n\nRuns the quality gate on each part and stops the build on a failure, naming the part to fix and how to rerun it."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2997",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2992"
              },
              "name": "Join planner",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg silencedetect\n\nMeasures each part's first and last word and keeps leadS before and tailS after them, so joins are trimmed by measurement rather than by hand-picked times."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2998",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2992"
              },
              "name": "Joiner",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg xfade + acrossfade\n\nChains a crossfade between every pair of parts, video and audio together."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2999",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2992"
              },
              "name": "Joined gate",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: qa.mjs --cues none\n\nWhole-video checks on the result, with the first part intro card and the last part outro card left out."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3000",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2992"
              },
              "name": "Video state recorder",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: memory.mjs recordVideo · video sync\n\nOn every way a build ends (built, failed the quality gate, failed outright) records the outcome, scope and qa counts in the video state file next to its page, and sends it to Zep."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3001",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2992"
              },
              "name": "Build report",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: build.json\n\nThe trims and every verdict, beside the parts."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClassDiagram",
              "_id": "c4-dgm-3002",
